  "worked_solution": "Consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=-2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"gretaer than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
